  "version": "0.1.0",
  "lastUpdated": "2026-08-11",
  "notes": [
    "The index of every value this app tracks. Metadata ONLY — no reference intakes, no descriptive copy. Those live in nutrients.json and nowhere else; splitting reference values across two files is how they drift apart.",
    "An id present here but absent from nutrients.json means the reference panel has not been written yet. The UI renders that as an explicit awaiting-data state rather than a blank or a zero, so this file doubles as the progress tracker for the remaining entries.",
    "Every id in nutrients.json must appear here. scripts/validate-data.mjs enforces that, and also enforces that every interactions[].with target resolves to a roster id.",
    "fdcNutrientId is null except where nutrients.json already establishes one. Hand-transcribed FoodData Central nutrient numbers are the same trap as hand-written fdcIds — a wrong number silently joins to the wrong nutrient. The Phase 0 importer fills these in.",
    "PLAN.md describes Tier 1 as 16 values but enumerates 18: it counts 'Fiber (total, soluble, insoluble)' as one line. This file lists all 18 separately, so the true roster is 59 values, not 57. Logged in docs/STATUS.md.",
    "storage drives the alert window and is a required field (CLAUDE.md rule 7). For Tier 1 values that are never deficiency-alerted it is set to the physiologically honest answer anyway rather than a placeholder."
  ],

